<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tissa Wewa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tissa Wewa is an ancient irrigation reservoir at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tissamaharama">Tissamaharama</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>. Built in the early centuries of the kingdom of Ruhuna, it watered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> fields of the dry south-east and is still in use. It is one of the oldest of the many tanks that sustained the early hydraulic civilisation of Sri Lanka.</p></div>
